# ── The undelivered marker, run against the child with nobody ────────────────
# The refused marker (counterfactual/undelivered-marker) is the alarm that would
# notice a person owed food who has not eaten. It fires on Nell — and it fires
# on everyone else alive in the record for the same reason, because `eats` is
# asserted for nobody. It is exactly right about the child and discriminates
# nothing, which is why the 2026-08-02 ruling refused it while the record holds
# no arrival facts. The one person it does not reach is the one it does not owe.
:expect-pins 4

? owe(State, Eats, Nell).
# => TRUE
? eats(Nell).
# => FALSE
? err(Nell, Undelivered).
# => TRUE
? err(Ori, Undelivered).
# => FALSE
